'' -m32 IS REFUSED, on every target and in either argument order. x86-64 is the only
'' architecture (D14), so there is no 32-bit target left to select.
''
'' Until 2026-09-04 this test asserted the OPPOSITE -- that -m32 selected win32 -- and
'' a separate test asserted that Linux refused it. The refusal is the whole behaviour
'' now, so the two are one test.
''
'' IT MUST BE AN ERROR RATHER THAN AN IGNORED FLAG: silently handing a 64-bit binary
'' to someone who asked for 32 is worse than telling them.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-types -m32 tests/source/plain.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 2
'' EXPECT-OUT: TKO0104: 32-bit targets are not supported; x86-64 only
